        "sections": [
          {
            "heading": "Practical structure",
            "content": "Treat the story like a short elevator pitch built from roughly one to seven statements. Use the progression “once upon a time,” “every day,” “one day,” and then “because of that” to connect what happened and where it led. Moesta describes the structure as a way to convey your core skills, the reason you changed, and the journey toward where you want to go. Keep it concise rather than explaining every detail.",
            "citation_ids": [
